    <annotation id="prefigure-potential-steps-figure" speech2="A flow diagram with three rows, one for each component of the vector field. Each row starts with a partial derivative condition in a blue box and ends with an updated formula for f. Row one: partial f partial x equals y z leads, by integrating in x, to x y z plus g of y and z. Row two: partial f partial y equals x z forces partial g partial y equals zero, giving x y z plus h of z. Row three: partial f partial z equals x y plus 2 z forces h prime of z equals 2 z, giving the final answer x y z plus z squared plus C in a vermillion box.">
